fix(transcode): MAX-RIGOR pass — orientation-aware 1080p cap

Pass-1 of the FINAL maximum-rigor 4-pass audit found that the C.1
1080p cap only worked correctly for landscape video. Portrait iPhone
4K (2160w × 3840h) re-encoded as 1920w × 3413h — width capped,
height proportionally ballooned, file ~2.5x the intended target.

Math:
  scale='min(1920,iw)':'-2'
    iw=2160, ih=3840
    w' = min(1920, 2160) = 1920  (downscale width)
    h' = -2 = auto = (ih * w' / iw) = 3840 * 1920 / 2160 = 3413
    output: 1920 x 3413  (NOT 1080 x 1920 as intended)

Fix: branch on orientation, cap whichever edge is the longer one:
  landscape (iw > ih)  → w = min(1920, iw), h = -2
  portrait/square      → w = -2,           h = min(1920, ih)

Verified:
  3840 x 2160 (landscape 4K)      → 1920 x 1080   ✓
  2160 x 3840 (portrait 4K iPhone)→ 1080 x 1920   ✓
  1280 x 720  (already <= cap)    → 1280 x 720    ✓ (no upscale)
   720 x 1280 (portrait 720p)     →  720 x 1280   ✓ (no upscale)
  2160 x 2160 (square 4K)         → 1920 x 1920   ✓

The remux fast-path for already-H.264 sources is untouched — no
scale filter applied, files served at native resolution.

Passes after fix:
  Pass 1 (wiring) — clean. Filter expression valid ffmpeg syntax.
  Pass 2 (real-time) — clean. Cron path unchanged; realtime UPDATE
    on social_posts is pre-existing INSERT-only gap (not regression).
  Pass 3 (adversarial) — clean. Filename passed to ffmpeg as separate
    arg (no shell injection). Max output bounded at 1920x1920.
  Pass 4 (edge cases) — clean. Equal w/h handled by ih branch.
    Sources <= cap not upscaled. 8K → 1920 max edge.
